<title>FINLAND: Finland sees Moody's current markka rating in EMU.</title>
<headline>Finland sees Moody's current markka rating in EMU.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Aaa domestic currency debt rating -- its highest -- for Finland is likely to remain the same for borrowing in euro if Finland joins Economic and Monetary Union, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is very likely that Moody's new rating will be held for the state's euro borrowing starting in 1999 if advances in economic policy and efforts to balance government finance follow the government programme,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-9-6805 0245</p>
